WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.840
What do you need to know about Marvel's Living&nbsp;
Vampire before he makes his big-screen debut?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.880
Who's in the cast? Who's directing? Keep watching&nbsp;
to find out everything we know about "Morbius."

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.680
"Morbius" was originally set to release in&nbsp;
the summer of 2020, right in the middle of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:20.800
blockbuster season alongside other major comic&nbsp;
book releases like "Black Widow" and "Eternals."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.840
That was a bold choice, but like the rest of the&nbsp;
2020 summer movie season, the pandemic got in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.720
way, and Sony moved its Living Vampire&nbsp;
back to the spring of 2021. Eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.560
spring became winter, and the film was bumped up&nbsp;
to its current release date of January 28, 2022.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.960
Filling the lead role of Dr. Michael Morbius is&nbsp;
Jared Leto. While he's known for his sometimes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.080
questionable commitment to his&nbsp;
roles, we haven't heard stories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.240
of any weird hijinks on the "Morbius"&nbsp;
set just yet. What we do know, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.920
is that Leto was already a big fan of&nbsp;
vampire stories when he took the role.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.320
Leto has a long history of consuming&nbsp;
vampire-centered media of various stripes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.640
and has a lot of passion for the genre, from&nbsp;
Anne Rice's "Interview with the Vampire" to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.680
Bram Stoker's original classic, "Dracula." It'll&nbsp;
be very interesting to see how he brings those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:12.800
influences to the comic book world of Morbius,&nbsp;
who's a unique vampire character in his own right.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.920
"I love the opportunity to do&nbsp;
something transformational."

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.520
Adria Arjona has been cast as Martine&nbsp;
Bancroft, Morbius' fiancee. As a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.240
supporting character to the Living Vampire,&nbsp;
who is himself generally not a leading man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.480
it's no surprise that there isn't exactly a&nbsp;
wealth of knowledge about her to glean from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.600
the source material. In the comics stories, she&nbsp;
often exists purely to die or be mind-controlled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:40.320
into joining cults, giving Morbius sorrow to&nbsp;
brood over until she's resurrected again. At one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.880
point she also tried to become a true mythical&nbsp;
vampire and turned on her lover before dying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.520
seemingly for good. In this case, though, the&nbsp;
fact that this lesser-known comic property&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:53.360
doesn't have an expansive lore could&nbsp;
actually work in the project's favor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:56.160
because it leaves room for a lot&nbsp;
of new invention in the story.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:01.040
Arjona herself may not be a household name,&nbsp;
but she's already got an impressive list of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.080
credits to her name going into "Morbius."&nbsp;
You may have already seen her in shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.840
like "True Detective" and "Good Omens"&nbsp;
and films like "Pacific Rim: Uprising."

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:13.520
Matt Smith has been cast as the key villain&nbsp;
of "Morbius," his best-friend-turned-enemy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:18.800
Loxias Crown, who also suffers from the same blood&nbsp;
disease as the Living Vampire. We don't know much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:23.680
about the motivations of this character played by&nbsp;
the former Time Lord, but the disease is fatal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.560
so Crown certainly has a lot of desperate&nbsp;
motivation to become the creature Morbius is.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:33.200
In the comics, Crown also goes by the villain name&nbsp;
Hunger. The character has only appeared in only a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:38.720
few comics, but he too is a pseudo-vampire created&nbsp;
by capturing Morbius and experimenting on him to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:44.720
gain his powers. Loxias could possibly be a blend&nbsp;
of this villain and Morbius' comics research&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.840
assistant Emil Nikos. We'll have to wait and see&nbsp;
how the comics and the film blend on this one.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:55.280
Two casting choices for Morbius' supporting&nbsp;
characters have piqued our curiosity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.280 --> 00:03:00.400
Tyrese Gibson, cast as an FBI agent referred&nbsp;
to as "Agent Stroud," is tasked with chasing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:05.040
Morbius down in the wake of his vampiric&nbsp;
killing spree. Then there's "Mad Men" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.840
"Chernobyl" star Jared Harris, who has been&nbsp;
cast as someone described as Morbius' mentor.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.560
The first trailer for "Morbius"&nbsp;
arrived in January 2020, with the dark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.320
brooding mood you might expect —&nbsp;
plus a few interesting surprises.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:21.920
Overall, the trailer summarizes&nbsp;
Morbius' motivation for the film:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:27.680
he's terminally ill and desperate to find a cure,&nbsp;
permitting Jared Leto to get very broody with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:33.840
performance. Hubris is an underlying theme, too,&nbsp;
with several shots of Morbius receiving awards yet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:38.720
feeling unsatisfied with the slow progression of&nbsp;
his research. That's what drives him to undertake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:44.880
the absurd steps he does to cure himself with&nbsp;
bats, no matter what his mentor or colleagues say.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:49.520
There are a few intriguing revelations to be&nbsp;
found in the first Morbius trailer — including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:54.000
a Spider-Man Easter egg and the return of&nbsp;
Michael Keaton's Vulture — but the biggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:59.120
surprise might be the revelation that the&nbsp;
source of Morbius' vampirism seems far more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:04.720
mystical than fans perhaps anticipated. He has&nbsp;
a weird-looking ceremonial knife and everything.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.440
Beyond that, we also get&nbsp;
glimpses of Martine Bancroft,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:10.400
who's been upgraded to Morbius'&nbsp;
research assistant for the film.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:16.880
Sony Pictures describes "Morbius" as a "horror&nbsp;
action story" about a scientist trying to cure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:21.760
his own rare blood disease. In the process,&nbsp;
he accidentally turns himself into a vampire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:26.080
Desperate for blood, he decides to feed&nbsp;
on criminals rather than innocent people.

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:30.160
In comics continuity, Dr. Michael Morbius&nbsp;
attempts to cure his rare blood disease&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:34.560
by inventing a serum distilled from the vital&nbsp;
fluids of bats, then hooking up to an electric&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:40.640
line to shock himself. As you might expect, this&nbsp;
harebrained idea goes a bit awry and whoops, now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:47.120
Dr. Morbius is a sci-fi vampire. That's why he's&nbsp;
the Living Vampire, you see — because science.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:51.520
From there, Morbius' transformation will make&nbsp;
a hero to some, and a villain to others, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:55.034
it's not clear how he himself&nbsp;
will get through it all…yet.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:00.880
At the helm of "Morbius" is Daniel Espinosa,&nbsp;
who was attached at virtually the same time Leto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:06.560
joined the project. His most recognizable director&nbsp;
credit in the United States is for the 2017 alien&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:12.000
horror-thriller "Life," but that's not his only&nbsp;
work. In his native Sweden he directed the 2010&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:16.960
film "Easy Money," and his other American&nbsp;
credits include "Safe House" and "Child 44."

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.480
On the writing side of things, Matt Sazama&nbsp;
and Burk Sharpless handled the script for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:24.880
"Morbius" after years of working together on&nbsp;
other genre projects. Their previous credits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:30.160
include "Gods of Egypt," the 2017 "Power&nbsp;
Rangers" reboot, and "Dracula Untold."

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:34.880
We know that "Morbius" is set in the&nbsp;
still-developing Sony Pictures universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:39.760
of Spider-Man supporting characters, but just how&nbsp;
much will it connect to other Spider-franchises?

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:44.560
Aside from a glimpse of Horizon Labs — a fun&nbsp;
Easter egg for comics readers who'll recognize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:48.560
the company where Peter Parker used to work&nbsp;
— the final "Morbius" trailer also makes it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.560 --> 00:05:53.680
clear that the title character very much shares a&nbsp;
universe with Spidey. We have an Oscorp sighting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.320
affirming that Green Goblin Norman Osborn&nbsp;
exists in this MCU-adjacent corner of reality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.960
and we also get another look at whatever's&nbsp;
going down when Adrian Toomes, aka The Vulture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:07.440
meets up with Morbius. There's also a Daily&nbsp;
Bugle headline touting Morbius' arrest amid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:09.920
references to other Spider-Man characters.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.000
"There's a web of opportunity."

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:16.880
This almost certainly only scratches the surface&nbsp;
of what we can expect in terms of connections&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:21.120
between the various Spider-franchises,&nbsp;
and we can't wait to see what's in store.

